    "narrative": "The anchor of today's lineup is **Corbin Carroll**, who commands the highest score (85.94) against Lowder. The combination of an elite batting order spot (#2) and an opponent with a slow delivery provides an ideal green light for **Corbin Carroll** to exploit the base paths, our most critical category for 5x5 leverage. Similarly, **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) is a standout play. While Bibee is a respectable arm, **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive park boost and high-efficiency platoon splits. The model also suggests keeping a close eye on **Gabriel Moreno** (70.08), as his integration into the #3 spot against the hittable Lowder elevates him into the elite tier of daily starters.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Cole Young**, who fell just shy of the threshold to displace our lower-tier starters. While **Cole Young** maintains a stable profile, the optimizer opted for the higher upside of **Brice Turang** (66.34), whose favorable matchup against P\u00e9rez and prime #2 lineup position created a clearer path to volume. Conversely, we are steering clear of **Jose Caballero** and **Austin Riley** today; both face daunting matchups against elite arms (Cease and Henderson, respectively) with xERAs well below 3.00. While the raw talent is present, their adjusted scores of 41.62 and 41.44 are simply too fragile to justify the risk of depleting our daily games remaining.\n\nLooking across the rest of the board, **Isaac Paredes** (61.73) remains a high-value play despite a subpar park, largely because his elite historical BvP against Lopez allows him to transcend the platoon disadvantage. We also see meaningful contributions expected from **Seiya Suzuki** (69.65), who grades out as a strong start despite the ballpark penalty. As always, the status of **James Wood** remains unchanged while he navigates his IL stint. We will monitor the official confirmation for **Max Muncy**, who carries the lowest score of our active starters (51.94) due to his #9 position; should the lineup shift, we may see a slight uptick in his efficiency, but for now, he serves as the floor for our infield depth.",
